known_false_positives.description:
**Missing Cleanup: isDefrag flag not reset on error paths**

The `commandBuffer->isDefrag` flag is set to 1 at the start of the defrag function (line 10605), but it's never explicitly reset. This flag persists on the command buffer object.

While this may be acceptable if the command buffer is released/recycled after use, it would be safer to reset the flag at the end of the function (around line 10775) to ensure clean state:

```c
SDL_UnlockMutex(renderer->allocatorLock);

commandBuffer->isDefrag = 0;
return true;
```

Also consider resetting it in error paths before returning false.
